                <a href="#fix-all-dev" class="doc-navlink">Fix all dev</a>
                <a href="#zero-naming" class="doc-navlink">zero.{domain}</a>
                <a href="#hosts" class="doc-navlink">Key hosts</a>
                <a href="#tools" class="doc-navlink">Tool roles</a>
                <a href="#identity" class="doc-navlink">Identity</a>
                <a href="#work" class="doc-navlink">Work items</a>
                <a href="#project-tracking" class="doc-navlink">Project tracking</a>
                <a href="#see-also" class="doc-navlink">See also</a>
            </div>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="now" class="doc-h2">Now</h2>
            <ul class="doc-body">
                <li><strong>Current.</strong> WAN port forward of workstation :3001 was disabled (2026-09-26). LAN <code>/health</code> on :3001 is 200. Public <code>computersystemconsulting.ca:3001</code> times out. Policy json is <code>config/infrastructure/gateway_plan.json</code> v1.2.</li>
                <li><strong>Blocked by.</strong> Single-thread Starman cannot be an internet origin. Public ZeroTier A records and a WAN HAProxy frontend would put the same worker back in the scanner queue.</li>
                <li><strong>Next.</strong> Named access for phones/laptops that have neither <code>/etc/hosts</code> nor ZeroTier (LAN = Unbound + mDNS; remote = authenticated HTTPS on 443, never :3001). Gateway audit must flag WAN DNAT/UPnP to .199:3001 as error.</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="overview" class="doc-h2">Overview</h2>
            <p class="doc-body">
                Canonical routing for CSC across OPNsense, Cloudflare, HAProxy, NPM, and application hosts.
                Live admin: <a class="doc-link" href="[% c.uri_for('/admin/infrastructure/opnsense') %]">OPNsense Gateway Management</a>.
                Policy file: <code>config/infrastructure/gateway_plan.json</code>.
            </p>
            <p class="doc-body">
                <code>dev.{domain}</code> is served by the workstation Starman
                (192.168.1.199 LAN / 172.30.131.126 ZeroTier), never production (192.168.1.126).
                That is a <strong>hostname</strong> policy. It is not a reason to publish TCP 3001 on the WAN.
            </p>
            <div class="doc-warning">
                <p><strong>2026-09-26.</strong> A WAN port forward TCP 3001 → 192.168.1.199 let scanners occupy the single <code>comserv_server.pl -r</code> worker (Recv-Q, multi-minute page loads). HAProxy on LAN :80 for <code>dev.computersystemconsulting.ca</code> was the intended design. The NAT was not.</p>
            </div>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="hard-rules" class="doc-h2">Hard rules</h2>
            <ul class="doc-body">
                <li><strong>No WAN DNAT of 3001</strong> (or UPnP / 1:1 / WAN pass to 192.168.1.199:3001). Bind <code>0.0.0.0</code> on the workstation is fine for LAN+ZT; it does not by itself publish the internet.</li>
                <li><strong>No public A record to a ZeroTier IP by default.</strong> RFC1918 in public DNS. Some resolvers strip it; visitors on 172.30 hit the wrong box. Keep Unbound, mDNS, and real ZT names.</li>
                <li><strong>Dev HAProxy frontend is LAN</strong> (or a later authenticated tunnel). Production HAProxy+ACME on WAN is a different role. Do not orange-cloud <code>dev.*</code> at the public IP:3001.</li>
                <li><strong>Gate ≠ app login.</strong> OPNsense / Access / client cert decides whether you may reach the host. Comserv session still owns SiteName and roles.</li>
                <li><strong>Starman on the desk is one worker.</strong> Public sockets or Recv-Q on 3001 is an incident, not “dev is up.”</li>
                <li><strong>Do not use</strong> <code>computersystemconsulting.ca:3001</code> as a URL. Use the names in <a href="#access">How to reach the app</a>.</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="access" class="doc-h2">How to reach the app</h2>
            <table class="doc-table">
                <tr>
                    <th class="doc-th">Client</th>
                    <th class="doc-th">DNS / name</th>
                    <th class="doc-th">URL</th>
                    <th class="doc-th">Notes</th>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td class="doc-td">Office LAN, DHCP uses OPNsense (192.168.1.1)</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">Unbound. No hosts file.</td>
                    <td class="doc-td"><code>http://dev.computersystemconsulting.ca/</code> (portless :80 → HAProxy → :3001). Other <code>dev.{zone}</code> need <code>:3001</code> until they share that frontend.</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">Default for phones and laptops on office Wi‑Fi.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr class="doc-tr-alt">
                    <td class="doc-td">Office LAN, mDNS</td>
                    <td class="doc-td"><code>workstation.local</code></td>
                    <td class="doc-td"><code>http://workstation.local:3001/</code></td>
                    <td class="doc-td">No hosts file. Avahi/Bonjour.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td class="doc-td">Office LAN, known IP</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">none</td>
                    <td class="doc-td"><code>http://192.168.1.199:3001/</code></td>
                    <td class="doc-td">Always works on this LAN.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr class="doc-tr-alt">
                    <td class="doc-td">ZeroTier member</td>
                    <td class="doc-td"><code>workstation.zero</code></td>
                    <td class="doc-td"><code>http://workstation.zero:3001/</code></td>
                    <td class="doc-td">Private overlay. Do not put 172.30.131.126 in Cloudflare.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td class="doc-td">Remote, no ZT, no hosts</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">Named HTTPS (not built yet)</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">See <a href="#nameless">No hosts file</a></td>
                    <td class="doc-td">Must not be WAN:3001 and must not be a public ZT A record.</td>
                </tr>
            </table>
            <p class="doc-body">Admin pages on the office LAN do not need ZeroTier. Cloudflare at <a class="doc-link" href="[% c.uri_for('/admin/dns') %]">/admin/dns</a> is a normal app page (admin login), not a VPN.</p>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="nameless" class="doc-h2">Devices with no hosts file</h2>
            <p class="doc-body">
                <code>/etc/hosts</code> is optional and local-only. Most phones, tablets, and guest laptops will never have it.
                They still need a <strong>name</strong>, not a ZeroTier address to type.
            </p>
            <h3 class="doc-h3">LAN (do this now)</h3>
            <ul class="doc-body">
                <li>DHCP DNS = 192.168.1.1 (Unbound). Specific <code>dev</code> host override beats zone wildcard.</li>
                <li><code>dev.computersystemconsulting.ca</code> → 192.168.1.1:80 → HAProxy → 192.168.1.199:3001.</li>
                <li><code>workstation.local</code> via mDNS for the raw Starman port.</li>
            </ul>
            <h3 class="doc-h3">Remote without ZeroTier (work item)</h3>
            <p class="doc-body">
                Build a named front door on <strong>443</strong> that authenticates, then proxies to 192.168.1.199:3001 on the LAN.
                Preferred: Cloudflare Tunnel + Access (or equivalent). Alternative: OPNsense HAProxy :443 with client certificate or IdP, origin still LAN.
                Staff who can install a client keep ZeroTier. Casual clients do not get a P12 in email as the only path.
            </p>
            <div class="doc-info">
                <p><strong>Rejected.</strong> Public DNS A = 172.30.131.126. That only works if the device is already on ZeroTier, and it publishes overlay addressing.</p>
            </div>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="fix-all-dev" class="doc-h2">What “Fix all dev.* → workstation” does</h2>
            <p class="doc-body">If the green button on the OPNsense admin page succeeds, it rewires <strong>names</strong>. It must not open WAN:3001.</p>
            <ul class="doc-body">
                <li>Unbound + HAProxy for <code>dev.computersystemconsulting.ca</code> (LAN :80 → workstation :3001).</li>
                <li>Unbound <code>dev.{other zone}</code> → 192.168.1.199.</li>
                <li>Today the code also writes Cloudflare A records to the workstation ZeroTier IP (DNS-only). <strong>That default is withdrawn in this plan</strong> — leave public <code>dev</code> unpublished until the 443 front door exists.</li>
                <li>Flashes an <code>/etc/hosts</code> snippet for machines that bypass Unbound. Optional. Not the LAN or remote design.</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="doc-body">Code: <code>Comserv::Util::GatewayOrchestrator::apply_all_dev_to_workstation</code>. WAN <code>add_port_forward</code> defaults in <code>Opnsense.pm</code> are a foot-gun; do not use them for Starman.</p>
            <p class="doc-body">Customer subdomains are not stored one-by-one in the json. <code>GatewayOrchestrator</code> builds rules from <code>hosting_accounts</code> when the gateway page loads. Audit flags <code>dev.*</code> shadowed by wildcard or pointing at production.</p>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="zero-naming" class="doc-h2">zero.{domain} — per site, not on the gateway</h2>
            <p class="doc-body">
                Each hosted domain may have <code>zero.{domain}</code> as a ZeroTier / remote entry hostname
                pointing at the <strong>application host</strong> (production1, a container, or the workstation), not OPNsense.
                That name is for members already on the overlay. It is not public internet access and should not be the Cloudflare default for people without ZeroTier.
            </p>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="hosts" class="doc-h2">Key hosts</h2>
            <table class="doc-table">
                <tr><th class="doc-th">Role</th><th class="doc-th">LAN</th><th class="doc-th">ZeroTier</th><th class="doc-th">Port</th></tr>
                <tr><td class="doc-td">OPNsense gateway</td><td class="doc-td">192.168.1.1</td><td class="doc-td">172.30.117.133</td><td class="doc-td">8443 (API)</td></tr>
                <tr class="doc-tr-alt"><td class="doc-td">production1 (Docker Catalyst)</td><td class="doc-td">192.168.1.126</td><td class="doc-td">172.30.50.206</td><td class="doc-td">5000</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="doc-td">Dev workstation</td><td class="doc-td">192.168.1.199</td><td class="doc-td">172.30.131.126</td><td class="doc-td">3001 (LAN/ZT only)</td></tr>
                <tr class="doc-tr-alt"><td class="doc-td">NPM (reverse proxy)</td><td class="doc-td">—</td><td class="doc-td">172.30.159.100</td><td class="doc-td">81 / 443</td></tr>
            </table>
            <p class="doc-body">See <a class="doc-link" href="[% c.uri_for('/Documentation/Server_Room_IP_Registry') %]">Server Room IP Registry</a>.</p>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="tools" class="doc-h2">Best tool per function</h2>
            <ul class="doc-body">
                <li><strong>OPNsense Unbound</strong> — LAN DNS so devices with no hosts file still resolve <code>dev.*</code> (and <code>dev.csc</code> to the gateway for portless HTTP).</li>
                <li><strong>OPNsense HAProxy</strong> — LAN :80 for <code>dev.computersystemconsulting.ca</code>. Production WAN HTTPS+ACME is a separate frontend.</li>
                <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong> — public DNS for internet-facing production names. Not for publishing workstation ZT or :3001.</li>
                <li><strong>NPM</strong> — per-container reverse proxy and certs for docker-delivered sites.</li>
                <li><strong>Tunnel + Access / client certs</strong> — remote people without ZeroTier; machines (AI API) use mTLS or tokens, not a cookie.</li>
                <li><strong>Comserv Gateway Plan</strong> — declared rules, drift vs live Unbound, this document.</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="doc-body">Unbound: a specific host override (<code>dev</code> + domain) beats a wildcard (<code>*</code> + domain).</p>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="identity" class="doc-h2">Identity: OPNsense vs Comserv</h2>
            <p class="doc-body">OPNsense is the door (VPN group, HAProxy client cert, Access). Comserv is the room (session, SiteName, roles). Stack them. Do not store shop vs accounting RBAC in OPNsense users.</p>
            <p class="doc-body">Client certificates: good for AI/API and a few known workers (<code>curl --cert</code>). They keep scanners off Starman if HAProxy verifies the cert on 443. They are a poor login for casual clients on a phone.</p>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="work" class="doc-h2">Work items</h2>
            <p class="doc-muted">Named items (not numbered phases). Owner project <a class="doc-link" href="[% c.uri_for('/project/details') %]?project_id=87">#87 Gateway</a>.</p>
            <table class="doc-table">
                <tr><th class="doc-th">Item</th><th class="doc-th">Gate (done when)</th><th class="doc-th">Todo</th></tr>
                <tr>
                    <td class="doc-td">WAN :3001 closed</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">No Port Forward / UPnP / 1:1 to .199:3001. Public connect to WAN:3001 fails. Recv-Q 0 unless LAN/ZT.</td>
                    <td class="doc-td"><a class="doc-link" href="[% c.uri_for('/todo/details') %]?record_id=2511">#2511</a> DONE 2026-09-26 (audit still #2505)</td>
                </tr>
                <tr class="doc-tr-alt">
                    <td class="doc-td">Gateway audit flags public Starman</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">OPNsense admin shows error if NAT/UPnP/WAN pass publishes 3001.</td>
                    <td class="doc-td"><a class="doc-link" href="[% c.uri_for('/todo/details') %]?record_id=2505">#2505</a> NEW P2</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td class="doc-td">Stop Cloudflare ZT A as default</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">Cloudflare sync does not write 172.30.131.126. “Fix all dev” does not create those records.</td>
                    <td class="doc-td"><a class="doc-link" href="[% c.uri_for('/todo/details') %]?record_id=2506">#2506</a> NEW P2</td>
                </tr>
                <tr class="doc-tr-alt">
                    <td class="doc-td">LAN names without hosts</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">Phone on office Wi‑Fi opens <code>http://dev.computersystemconsulting.ca/</code> with only DHCP DNS. mDNS <code>workstation.local:3001</code> works.</td>
                    <td class="doc-td"><a class="doc-link" href="[% c.uri_for('/todo/details') %]?record_id=2507">#2507</a> NEW P4</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td class="doc-td">Remote named access (no ZT, no hosts)</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">A hostname on 443 with Access/IdP/client-cert reaches workstation :3001. Document the URL. No WAN:3001.</td>
                    <td class="doc-td"><a class="doc-link" href="[% c.uri_for('/todo/details') %]?record_id=2508">#2508</a> NEW P3</td>
                </tr>
                <tr class="doc-tr-alt">
                    <td class="doc-td">Client certs for machine API</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">HAProxy or app verifies certs for AI/ingest; scanners without cert never hit Starman.</td>
                    <td class="doc-td"><a class="doc-link" href="[% c.uri_for('/todo/details') %]?record_id=2509">#2509</a> NEW P5</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td class="doc-td">Foot-gun: WAN add_port_forward</td>
                    <td class="doc-td"><code>Opnsense.pm</code> does not default interface WAN / dest wan:ip / port 3001 for Comserv dev.</td>
                    <td class="doc-td"><a class="doc-link" href="[% c.uri_for('/todo/details') %]?record_id=2510">#2510</a> NEW P2</td>
                </tr>
                <tr class="doc-tr-alt">
                    <td class="doc-td">ROUTINE re-audit</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">Plan still matches live NAT/Unbound/HAProxy/Cloudflare; :3001 not on WAN.</td>
                    <td class="doc-td"><a class="doc-link" href="[% c.uri_for('/todo/details') %]?record_id=2512">#2512</a> recurring P10</td>
                </tr>
            </table>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="project-tracking" class="doc-h2">Project tracking</h2>
            <div class="doc-success">
                <p>
                    <a class="doc-link" href="[% c.uri_for('/project/details') %]?project_id=87">Open project #87 (Gateway)</a>
